{"name":"Dry Dune","hex":"#efdfcf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Darai."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Free from or lacking moisture.","Unable to produce a liquid, as water,  oil, or  milk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dry"},{"term":"dune","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ridge or hill of sand piled up by currents of wind or water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dune"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dune","blocks":[{"text":"A dune is a landform composed of wind- or water-driven sand. It typically takes the form of a mound, ridge, or hill. An area with dunes is called a dune system or a dune complex. A large dune complex is called a dune field, while broad, flat regions covered with wind-swept sand or dunes, with little or no vegetation, are called ergs or sand seas. Dunes occur in different shapes and sizes, but most kinds of dunes are longer on the stoss (upflow) side, where the sand is pushed up the dune, and have a shorter slip face in the lee side. The valley or trough between dunes is called a dune slack."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Dunas_de_Maspalomas.jpg/330px-Dunas_de_Maspalomas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dune","wikidata":"Q25391"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Saltation_on_sand_dune.png/330px-Saltation_on_sand_dune.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Saltation_on_sand_dune.png/330px-Saltation_on_sand_dune.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sand hitting sand is more likely to stick; sand hitting a more coherent surface is more likely to bounce (saltation). This exacerbating feedback loop helps sand accumulate into dunes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaltation_on_sand_dune.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Barchan_in_Noachis.jpg/330px-Barchan_in_Noachis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Barchan_in_Noachis.jpg/330px-Barchan_in_Noachis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Isolated barchan dunes on the surface of Mars. Dominant wind direction would be from left to right.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarchan_in_Noachis.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg/250px-Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg/500px-Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg/250px-Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARub'_al_Khali_(Arabian_Empty_Quarter)_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_(EOS_AM-1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/ISS-31_Linear_dunes_in_the_Great_Sand_Sea_in_southwest_Egypt.jpg/500px-ISS-31_Linear_dunes_in_the_Great_Sand_Sea_in_southwest_Egypt.jpg?utm_source=en.w